y</given-names></name><name><surname>Marc</surname><given-names>SMangel</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>amei: Adaptive Management of Epidemiological Interventions. R package version 1.0.</article-title><comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/amei/index.html">http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/amei/index.html</ext-link></comment></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005807-Hetchote1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hetchote</surname><given-names>HW</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>The mathematics of infectious diseases.</article-title><source>SIAM Review</source><volume>42</volume><fpage>599</fpage><lpage>653</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005807-McCallum1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McCallum</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Barlow</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Hone</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>How should pathogen transmission be modelled?</article-title><source>Trends in Ecology and Evolution</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>295</fpage><lpage>300</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11369107</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005807-Clark1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>CW</given-names></name><name><surname>Mangel</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><source>Dynamic State Variable Models in Ecology: Methods and Applications.</source><publisher-name>Oxford University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005807-Gamerman1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surn